        <a class="cond-chip" href={href}>{label}</a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
     §4 HOW TREATMENT WORKS — dark
═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section-dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" style="max-width:52ch">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">Your First Visit</p>
      <h2>How Tui Na Treatment Works</h2>
      <p style="color:rgba(240,234,226,0.75)">Diagnosis before treatment at every appointment. Nothing repeated by habit.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="journey-grid">
      <div class="journey-step">
        <div class="j-num">01</div>
        <h3>Clinical Assessment</h3>
        <p>
          20 minutes allocated to full clinical assessment before any hands-on treatment.
          Chief complaint, orthopaedic movement testing, and TCM pattern identification.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="journey-step">
        <div class="j-num">02</div>
        <h3>Targeted Treatment</h3>
        <p>
          Technique selection is based on your clinical findings — not a routine protocol.
          Measurable goals are set at the start. Discharge criteria agreed in advance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="journey-step">
        <div class="j-num">03</div>
        <h3>Progress Review</h3>
        <p>
          Follow-up sessions begin with a brief progress check — what changed since last
          session? Technique is adjusted accordingly. No sessions on autopilot.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:2.5rem;text-align:center">
      <a class="btn btn-gold" href="https://wa.me/447301949686" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Book Your First Consultation</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
     §5 CLINICAL APPROACH
═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section-soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid-2-lg" style="gap:5rem">

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Our Approach</p>
        <h2>Tui Na at Yin Yang CMC</h2>

        <div class="pull-quote">
          <p>"Technique follows diagnosis, not habit. Every session adapted to your
          current clinical picture."</p>
        </div>

        <p>
          Our practitioners apply Tui Na using specific technique sequences from the
          Hong Kong clinical curriculum — not a generalised massage approach. The
          distinction matters clinically: wrong technique applied to the right area
          can delay recovery.
        </p>

        <p>
          For structural presentations, Tui Na is frequently staged alongside bone
          setting — soft tissue mobilisation first, then joint mobilisation. For
          injury recovery, the technique shifts across the three phases of tissue
          healing (acute, sub-acute, remodelling).
        </p>

        <details class="expand-detail">
          <summary class="expand-summary">
            Three mechanisms of Tui Na
            <span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="expand-body">
            <h3>Myofascial release</h3>
            <p>
              Directional pressure is used to ease fascial tightness and support range of
              motion in restricted joints. This is distinct from general massage pressure,
              which targets surface muscle tension rather than the fascial layer.
            </p>
            <h3>Neurological regulation</h3>
            <p>
              Rhythmic compression activates mechanoreceptors, downregulating the stress
              response and reducing referred pain. This mechanism explains why Tui Na
              produces effects beyond the site of manual contact.
            </p>
            <h3>Meridian &amp; circulatory support</h3>
            <p>
              Supporting meridian flow — a model that maps closely onto microcirculation
              and lymphatic drainage. Particularly relevant in recovery from acute injury,
              where local swelling can slow tissue healing.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div style="display:grid;gap:1.5rem;align-content:start">
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:var(--border);border-radius:var(--r-lg);overflow:hidden">
          {[
            { val: "MBAcC",  label: "BAcC Registered" },
            { val: "15+",    label: "Years' Experience" },
            { val: "60m",    label: "First Appointment" },
            { val: "EN/粵",  label: "Bilingual Care" },
